          "text": "{\"target_identification\":{\"speaker\":\"Lorck\",\"addressee\":\"Constance\",\"anchor_quote\":\"Jeg elsker dig, Constance  det er Alvor,\\nganske anderledes end jeg selv endog vidste.\\nJeg giver dig mig selv, mit Liv, min Sjæl, -\\nvil du ikke ta imod det?\"},\"target_translation\":\"I love you.\",\"dimensions\":{\"T\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.99,\"reason\":\"The focal expression directly avows, as true, Lorck's present loving emotional state toward Constance. His immediate insistence that it is serious reinforces its truth-presenting force, regardless of whether every associated claim is sincere.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"Jeg elsker dig\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Jeg elsker dig, Constance  det er Alvor\"}]},\"P\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.97,\"reason\":\"The focal words themselves do not undertake a future act, obligation, or defined relationship; they avow a state. Lorck's immediately following offer of himself, his life, and his soul is a separate neighbouring relational offer and must not be transferred onto the marked expression. Constance explicitly rejects that offer.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"Jeg elsker dig\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Jeg giver dig mig selv, mit Liv, min Sjæl, -\\nvil du ikke ta imod det?\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Nej, uf nej\"}]},\"E\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.94,\"reason\":\"Although Lorck is emotionally agitated, the focal expression is presented as a deliberate, serious avowal in an attempt to persuade Constance, not as a reflex-like cry or affective discharge. Emotional intensity alone does not establish E.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"Jeg elsker dig\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Lorck korsede Armene paa Brystet, og\\nbetragtede hende stift.\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"det er Alvor\"}]},\"O\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.93,\"reason\":\"The core force of the focal expression is adequately captured by T. Its contextual persuasive purpose does not constitute a distinct core mode beyond the avowal itself.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"Jeg elsker dig\"}]}},\"original_speech_situation\":\"In a private, escalating confrontation, Lorck has disclosed his passion and pressed Constance to yield to him. After she resists, asks him to stop, and reacts fearfully to his demand for an answer, he addresses her directly with the focal avowal and then makes a separate offer of himself, his life, and his soul. She rejects the offer and backs away.\",\"affection_evidence\":\"present\",\"undertaking_and_uptake\":\"The marked expression itself contains no undertaking. In the immediately following, distinct utterance, Lorck offers Constance himself, his life, and his soul and asks whether she will accept them. The precise practical or relational terms are unspecified. Constance refuses—“Nej, uf nej”—so there is no uptake of that offer. Narrative descriptions of his prolonged infatuation, bodily agitation, and later private attachment provide evidence of actual affection, though they do not validate his coercive conduct or every grandiose claim.\",\"recognised_work\":true,\"recognition_note\":\"Recognised as Amalie Skram's novel Constance Ring; the supplied material also explicitly prints the author and title.\",\"limitations\":\"The classification concerns only the marked occurrence of “Jeg elsker dig.” The adjacent offer is relevant context but is not part of TARGET. The supplied passages support affection and rejection, but they do not fully determine the sincerity or exact intended terms of Lorck's broader offer.\"}"
